From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: add QSDK NSS board DTS for spectrum_sbe1v1k

Adds the device tree the QSDK 14.x NSS data path needs, in two files under
target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ (copied into the
kernel tree by the quilt kernel-patch step):

  ipq9574-nss.dtsi       soc-level NSS nodes taken from the QSDK 14.x
                         ipq9574.dtsi: ess-instance/ess-switch (with the
                         port scheduler tables), edma@3ab00000 and nss-ppe.
                         qca-ssdk, qca-nss-dp and qca-nss-ppe each locate
                         these by name or compatible:
                           ssdk_dts.c:1526  of_find_node_by_name(NULL,"ess-instance")
                           edma_v3/edma.c:1711  of_find_node_by_name(NULL,"edma")
                           ppe_drv.c:5170   of_find_compatible_node(...,"qcom,nss-ppe")
                         Without the nss-ppe node ppe_drv_module_init() returns
                         -EINVAL and the PPE module refuses to load.

  ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts    the board file: mainline RDP433 hardware baseline
                         (PCIe, MDIO/PHY wiring, NOR/NAND, LEDs, keys) plus
                         the QSDK RDP433 switch topology and EDMA ring layout.

Two details worth calling out:

  - /delete-node/ &qcom_ppe;  The mainline PPE driver claims the same
    0x3a000000 window, and its child node is named "edma".  Because
    of_node_name_eq() (drivers/of/base.c:59) compares names with the unit
    address stripped, of_find_node_by_name(NULL,"edma") would match that
    mainline child instead of edma@3ab00000.

  - &mdio uses "phy-reset-gpio" (singular), which is what
    ssdk_dt_parse_mdio_node() (ssdk_dts.c:954) reads, not the phylib
    "reset-gpios" used by the mainline board file.

The board is not documented, so the switch/PHY assignments follow the QSDK
RDP433 reference (QCA8075 PSGMII on ports 1-4, AQR USXGMII on ports 5-6).
They are placeholders until real hardware evidence is available.

The device definition still points at ipq9574-rdp433: this DTS has no NSS
kmods in DEVICE_PACKAGES yet, and deleting the mainline PPE node without
them would leave the image without Ethernet.

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-nss.dtsi b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-nss.dtsi
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-nss.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-nss.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,572 @@
