+/*
+ * IPQ9574 NSS data path (QSDK 14.x) - SoC level device tree nodes
+ *
+ * The mainline 6.12 IPQ9574 device tree has no node for the NSS data path:
+ * QSDK 14.x keeps these in its own ipq9574.dtsi.  The three nodes carried
+ * here are copied from
+ *
+ *   qca/src/linux-6.6/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi   (QSDK 14.x)
+ *
+ * and are the ones the QSDK drivers actually consume:
+ *
+ *   ess-instance / ess-switch  qca-ssdk locates the switch with
+ *                              of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "ess-instance")
+ *                              then "ess-switch"; the scheduler tables are
+ *                              read by ssdk_dt_parse_scheduler_cfg().
+ *   edma@3ab00000               qca-nss-dp finds its ring configuration with
+ *                              of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "edma").
+ *   nss-ppe                    qca-nss-ppe refuses to initialise without a
+ *                              "qcom,nss-ppe" compatible node.
+ *
+ * Board files include this file and add the board specific pieces:
+ * switch_mac_mode*, qcom,port_phyinfo, the dpN (qcom,nss-dp) nodes and the
+ * EDMA ring layout.
+ *
+ * The mainline "ethernet@3a000000" (qcom,ipq9574-ppe) node must be deleted by
+ * the board before this file is used - it owns the same register window and
+ * also contains a child node named "edma", which would make the
+ * of_find_node_by_name() lookup above ambiguous.
+ *
+ * Status: compile tested only, NOT TESTED on hardware.
+ */
